<Legal title="Privacy Policy" updated="June 11, 2026">
  <p>
    Crossfade is a small tool that copies a public YouTube playlist to your
    Spotify account. It is designed to know as little about you as possible.
    This page explains exactly what it touches and what it doesn't.
  </p>

  <h2>What Crossfade accesses</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>YouTube:</strong> the title and track list of the public
      playlist you paste. Nothing about your YouTube or Google account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Spotify:</strong> after you connect your account, Crossfade can
      search the Spotify catalogue and create playlists on your behalf. That
      is the full extent of the permissions it requests.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Crossfade stores</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing, server-side. There is no database, no user accounts, and no
    analytics. The only data kept anywhere is in your own browser:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Spotify authentication tokens, stored as secure httpOnly cookies — an
      access token that expires within an hour, and a refresh token kept for
      up to 30 days so you don't have to reconnect each visit.
    </li>
    <li>
      The playlist URL you pasted, kept briefly in your browser's session
      storage so it survives the redirect through Spotify's login page.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Playlist data passes through the server only for the duration of each
    request and is never written down. Your data is never sold, shared, or
    used for anything beyond performing the conversion you asked for.
  </p>

  <h2>Disconnecting</h2>
  <p>
    Click <em>disconnect</em> in the header at any time — this deletes the
    authentication cookies from your browser. To fully revoke Crossfade's
    access to your Spotify account, you can also remove it at
    <a href="https://www.spotify.com/account/apps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      spotify.com/account/apps</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Crossfade uses YouTube API Services and the Spotify Web API. By using it
    you also agree to the
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      YouTube Terms of Service</a>; the
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Google Privacy Policy</a>
    and
    <a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Spotify Privacy Policy</a>
    apply to data those services process. Fonts are served by Google Fonts.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes &amp; contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date above will be updated. Questions:
    <a href="mailto:hey@davidumoru.me">hey@davidumoru.me</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
